{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1139760-homemade-city-and-consilium-2e","id":1139760,"title":"Homemade City and Consilium (2e)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-09-12T13:40:24-07:00","id":1139760,"title":"Homemade City and Consilium (2e)","content":"So a few years back I created a homemade city for me to set all my World of Darkness games in. It has gone through several iterations and recently I shifted it to my native Sweden.<br /> <br /> After playing a few sessions within the latest &quot;iteration&quot; with some friends I felt that while each Order has their own thing I felt that I wanted something more.<br /> <br /> I felt that in the same way as an individual Mage ground their own magic in some kind of magical tradition and symbolism, the local founder of the Order would ground the Order within the same symbolism that they use.<br /> <br /> This way, I would get an idea of what the Order in general act like and thus I can make them more obviously different. I also want to ground them somewhat in symbols and mysticism that could be found in Sweden, to give it a somewhat more local feeling.<br /> <br /> I was thinking:<br /> <br /> Silver Ladder: <i>Hermeticism </i>given that it is a idea that is somewhat associated with the upper-class and with scholars.<br /> <br /> Guardians of the Veil: <i>al-\u1e24ash\u0101sh\u012bn. </i>I know that this is not something that was around in Sweden, but my friends and I could not come up with ANY organization that was tied to Sweden and matched with the Guardians. Instead I thought I'd go with these as it would also lend a feeling of &quot;otherness&quot; to them.<br /> <br /> Adamantine Arrow: The Arrow have been the hardest ones actually. I was thinking of doing <i>Monastic Knights </i>at first, but my friends pointed out that Sweden has barely had any knightly tradition in the same way as the rest of Europe. Instead I was suggested doing them as <i>Vikings</i>. Yet we do have Germany just a bit south of here and their knightly traditions. So I'm having a hard time taking a pick.<br /> <br /> Mysterium: <i>Kabbalah and </i><i>Jewish Traditions </i>given the tradition of learning and discussing ideas and interpreting sacred texts.<br /> <br /> Free Council: A mix of <i>Nordic mysticism </i>and <i>Technomagic.</i> I do love me some technomagic.<br /> <br /> <br /> In the end I want your opinions. What do you guys think? Would you change any of them? Do you have suggestions? What should I settle on with the Arrow? Any other thoughts?<br /> <br /> I am very open to suggestions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I SHOOT THE GIGGLING!... What do I know about &quot;giggling&quot;?&quot;","edited":{"userid":1089,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1089-captainsl","user":"CaptainSL","date":". 09-12-2017, 04:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1089-captainsl","name":"CaptainSL","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1089_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-12T14:06:20-07:00","id":1139766,"title":"","content":"I'd have the Arrow concentrating on a syncretism of Germanic knighthood and Scandinavian Vikings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-12T14:09:11-07:00","id":1139767,"title":"","content":"I think that's a neat idea. Though, I'd keep in mind that the symbolism of local orders doesn't have to be a one-to-one. I mean, in Boston for example, the Guardians were associated with Hermeticsm, because that allowed them to create their labyrinths, there's not really a direct correlation with their beliefs (that's indeed kinda the point).<br /> <br /> Thinking about it, 'Nordic Mysticism' is generally about reconstructing or borrowing from religions that have been dead for many centuries, so there's plenty of room there for an enterprising Guardian. Indeed, maybe the Guardians (or any Diamond really) think they preserve a correct version from before christianisation, whilst the Free Council think the sleeper reconstructions are just as valid.<br /> <br /> For the Arrow, Sweden might not have had literal fighting orders, but there's a long tradition of Orders of knights in the more modern sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-12T23:17:13-07:00","id":1139841,"title":"","content":"Whatever you do with the Arrow I would recommend keeping the image of the Viking Feast Hall.<br /> \u200bIt not only contributes to a sense of brotherhood but would be appealing to potential recruits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}